{"title":"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 34","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_34\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 34</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(answer_choices,_no_AM-GM_or_calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (answer choices, no AM-GM or calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_34\">Problem 34</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 34\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/f/dff5a847457c4beaa2c6809fc9d7b26ebcaa398e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb2a198833ad9bafd53c554eae00fd8538041bf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {4x^2 + 8x + 13}{6(1 + x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"111\" height=\"43\" /> is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/3/393eaa0f78a2c30aec53ecb5f5be8bba083ffe8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1 \\qquad  \\textbf{(B) }\\ 2 \\qquad  \\textbf{(C) }\\ \\frac {25}{12} \\qquad  \\textbf{(D) }\\ \\frac{13}{6}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\ \\frac{34}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"412\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To begin, lets denote the equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb2a198833ad9bafd53c554eae00fd8538041bf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {4x^2 + 8x + 13}{6(1 + x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"111\" height=\"43\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />. Let's notice that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e05e5dce0a1cfbf9ca17efa00fb2c6c2fb7dcb3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f(x) &amp; = \\frac {4x^2 + 8x + 13}{6(1 + x)}\\\\\\\\ \t &amp; = \\frac{4(x^2+2x) + 13}{6(x+1)}\\\\\\\\      &amp; = \\frac{4(x^2+2x+1-1)+13}{6(x+1)}\\\\\\\\      &amp; = \\frac{4(x+1)^2+9}{6(x+1)}\\\\\\\\      &amp; = \\frac{4(x+1)^2}{6(x+1)} + \\frac{9}{6(1+x)}\\\\\\\\      &amp; = \\frac{2(x+1)}{3} + \\frac{3}{2(x+1)}\\\\\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"247\" height=\"426\" />\n</p><p>After this simplification, we may notice that we may use calculus, or the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM inequality\">AM-GM inequality</a> to finish this problem because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b5205f058a0f55b22ecf025f21108e6b2ed1100c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, which implies that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f5c44cedc405fd48d79549e9b88240deaac2a0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2(x+1)}{3} \\text{ and } \\frac{3}{2(x+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"173\" height=\"43\" /> are greater than zero. Continuing with AM-GM:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bf32ab6d88d4e97a3e22c8b4e0350b0838c2267.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{\\frac{2(x+1)}{3} + \\frac{3}{2(x+1)}}{2} &amp;\\ge {\\small \\sqrt{\\frac{2(x+1)}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2(x+1)}}}\\\\\\\\ f(x) &amp;\\ge 2 \\end{align*}\" width=\"308\" height=\"103\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aeebf4cfe56a7ea9b5b522e9d9b20f6aa6fcfc88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\frac {4x^2 + 8x + 13}{6(1 + x)} \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"208\" height=\"45\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" /> \n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/8/e58787371eac9d80069c7fe6e4dc2a2c5ba86a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\text{With equality when } \\frac{2(x+1)}{3} = \\frac{3}{2(x+1)}, \\text{ or } x=\\frac{1}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"406\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Calculus)\">Solution 2 (Calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/5/21510e0a814a0f5810771cb80fd1e554313af78c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\frac{4x^2 + 8x + 13}{6(1 + x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"174\" height=\"45\" />.\nTake the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Derivative\" title=\"Derivative\">derivative</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quotient_rule\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Quotient rule\">quotient rule</a>.\n\\begin{align*} \nf(x) &amp;= \\frac{4x^2 + 8x + 13}{6(1 + x)} \\\\\nf'(x) &amp;= \\frac{1}{6}*\\frac{(4x^2 + 8x + 13)'(1 + x) - (4x^2 + 8x + 13)(1 + x)'}{(1 + x)^2} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{(8x + 8)(1 + x) - (4x^2 + 8x + 13)(1)}{6(1 + x)^2} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{4x^2 + 8x - 5}{6(1 + x)^2} \\\\\n\\end{align*}\nNext, set the numerator equal to zero to find the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-value of the minimum:\n\\begin{align*}\n4x^2+8x-5 &amp;= 0 \\\\ \n(2x+5)(2x-1) &amp;= 0 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\nFrom the problem, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44df9cb6ce6f056c64c197a004b64fc4dd3a5aa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, so we are left with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/4/a14649b556d4c316856b101be1b84a92084b195b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />. Plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/4/a14649b556d4c316856b101be1b84a92084b195b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\nf(\\frac{1}{2})&amp;=\\frac{4(\\frac{1}{2})^2+8(\\frac{1}{2})+13}{6(1+(\\frac{1}{2}))} \\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{1+4+13}{6(\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{18}{9} \\\\\n&amp;=2 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fee36265d80f955ca6b0c0efb730384788a1861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28answer_choices.2C_no_AM-GM_or_calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(answer_choices,_no_AM-GM_or_calculus)\">Solution 3 (answer choices, no AM-GM or calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (answer choices, no AM-GM or calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We go from A through E and we look to find the smallest value so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/f/dff5a847457c4beaa2c6809fc9d7b26ebcaa398e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, so we start from A:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c63667e6b9a093b2787d07b9e43547e06670f3c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4x^2 + 8x + 13}{6x+6} = 1\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/2892c9b21344f12df4b5f01905bd4b3a078a861b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x^2 + 8x + 13 = 6x + 6\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2cceff142b1580b08d030be6f0e54c3f8550a23.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x^2 + 2x + 7 = 0\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>However by the quadratic formula there are no real solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be greater than 0. We move on to B:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08a59b22b179a0f7c9fb394d496b431c219c96a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4x^2 + 8x + 13}{6x + 6} = 2\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/7/c3767053a78c01fcda29c0562ddece62565a0d7a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x^2 + 8x + 13 = 12x + 12\\]\" width=\"201\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/177e2f48b7cc5125153064feed9342f19860c4f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x^2 - 4x + 1 = 0\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bdd669f84ef28d129b0e3ca32552236da8c6ed9e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2x-1)^2 = 0\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>There is one solution: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2ff20448834be77dc325234211669d2b44d35aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />, which is greater than 0, so 2 works as a value. Since all the other options are bigger than 2 or invalid, the answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/7/c27f60ab9118fe60e2d0a4614c01f1e9824c2c5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{B}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME\" title=\"1965 AHSME\">1965 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1965 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1965\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 33\">Problem 33</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_35\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 35\">Problem 35</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 31\">31</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 32\">32</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 33\">33</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">34</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_35\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 35\">35</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_36\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 36\">36</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_37\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 37\">37</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 38\">38</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_39\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 39\">39</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 40\">40</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017164815\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.045 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.066 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 294/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2984/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 196/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6497/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.059      1 -total\n 62.66%    8.810      1 Template:AHSME_40p_box\n 35.16%    4.943      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18077:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017164815 and revision id 223138. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}